
  <sn><md>### Introduction to Sets

* **Everyday Context:** The word "set" is commonly used in daily life (e.g., a tea set, sofa set, dinner set, or set of books).
* **Historical Origin:** German mathematician [George Cantor](https://cdn.britannica.com/29/129929-004-45A7A5DD/Georg-Cantor.jpg) (1845–1918) introduced and detailed the mathematical concept of sets, establishing what is known as **Set Theory**.
*  &gt;  A **set** is a `well-defined collection of objects` from the real or abstract/imaginary world
* **Well-Defined Requirement:** It must be clear whether any given object belongs to the set or not.
* **Key Characteristics:**
	* Order does not matter.
	* Elements are `not repeated`.

